Gentles,

We've had a number of issues where someone has posted a post along the
lines of

>>> wow! that's really cool!

Followed by a response along the lines of

>> What's really cool?  How about some context, you stupid twit!

Followed by
> Why don't you get a modern newsreader, moron?

Etc.

Here is the problem, as I see it.  People on this group use newsreaders
with varying capabilities, for reasons of their own.  What is
completely obvious with a threaded newsreader is NOT obvious to a
traditional one.


And the above is just one example.  Another one is the fact that a
signature must be separated from the body of the message by two dashes
and a space.

And those are just the two I know about.  There are doubtless others,
which we )meaning those of us with threaded readers) can't know about
because -- again -- with our newsreaders we *just aren't aware of it*.


Therefore I propose the following solution:
1) We -- the nethack community -- agree on a common set of guidelines
that are specific to rec.games.roguelike.nethack. Something that
everyone, with all newsreaders, can agree on.

2) We publish it on a regular schedule, like the normal FAQ.

This way,  when people continually mess up, it isn't because of
ignorance but because of willful stupidity. For first-time offenders,
we point them to the FAQ.  Repeat offenders get killfiled (for those
who care).  It's a very different thing to disobey posted rules than it
is to break rules that are just assumed.

Why aren't the normal FAQs adequate?  Because, sad to say,  those FAQs
are outdated.  I myself have had trouble on this group -- but I have
ONLY had trouble here. I have posted on other groups for years without
a breath of complaint. Why?  Because many of the inhabitants of those
other groups use the same readers I do.  It simply wasn't an issue.

rec.games.roguelike.nethack is a unique community.  As such,  it
requires a unique FAQ.

